# Wine (CrossOver 26.2.0 source) — winemac.drv: conditional offscreen presentation for
# windows with visible child windows (ticket 001, T-23).
#
# Problem: under winemac a GL window is presented as a separate surface above the window's
# GDI content, so GDI child windows (CEF login/channel panels) are invisible.
# Fix: while a window has visible child windows, render into the (hidden) GL view, read the
# frame back and blit it into the window surface, clipping out the child windows; without
# visible children, present the GL view normally (no per-frame copy).  Environment-level
# only: no game/client files are touched.
#
# AI-assisted ("vibe-coded") during a real debugging session; workaround, no warranty, review before use.
# Build: ~/GameLab/build/cx-26.2.0-x11 (configures against ~/GameLab/src/cx-26.2.0/sources/wine)
#   make -j8 dlls/winemac.drv/winemac.so
#   cp dlls/winemac.drv/winemac.so ~/GameLab/wine-cx-x11/lib/wine/x86_64-unix/winemac.so
# Rollback: restore winemac.so.orig-T22 (kept next to the installed driver).
